    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Sell\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan calls for trimming AAPL exposure by roughly 25-35% to reduce risk while the stock trades below all major moving averages (10 EMA, 50 SMA, 200 SMA, VWMA) in a confirmed multi-timeframe downtrend approaching a death cross. The technical evidence is the most complete and decisively bearish: MACD histogram widening negatively, RSI at 36.18, relative volume of 1.27x on down days indicating distribution, and a 9.2% drawdown from the 60-day peak despite a $30.6B buyback. While the $39.9B quarterly operating cash flow supports long-term business strength, the plan explicitly states this is not a Buy and recommends trimming exposure rather than holding full position. The plan directs reducing existing exposure by 25-35% at current levels ($177.72) rather than initiating new longs, making a partial Sell the appropriate action to align with the underweight recommendation.\n\n**Entry Price**: 177.72\n\n**Stop Loss**: 170.0\n\n**Position Sizing**: Trim 25-35% of existing AAPL position\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **SELL**",
